pg:Q10_O1 a ld:AnswerOption ;
    rdfs:label "The fourth subject is control shared among keys and among people: multisignature signing and key loss, the odds of loss and theft, the bytes a script costs, and secret sharing, which the chapter does not mention (Antonopoulos ..."@en .

pg:Q10_O2 a ld:AnswerOption ;
    rdfs:label "Because a multisignature address depends on the set of keys, wallets must agree on their order, and BIP 67 solves it by sorting the public keys lexicographically by their binary form (Kerin et al., 2015)."@en .

pg:Q10_O3 a ld:AnswerOption ;
    rdfs:label "This section is about the words, the seed and the master key that follow from them, tested against the published vectors (Palatinus et al., 2013)."@en .

